.TH "lua\-pdfio" "3" "2026\-09\-20"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
lua\-pdfio \- Lua wrapper for the pdfio library
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
local pdfio = require("lua\-pdfio")
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBlua\-pdfio\fR is a Lua module that provides an interface to the \fBpdfio\fR library for
reading and writing PDF files.\& Most functions map directly onto their pdfio C
counterparts; see \fBpdfio\fR(3) for the underlying semantics.\&
.PP
.SH MODULE FUNCTIONS
.PP
\fBpdfio.\&open(filename [, password])\fR
.RS 4
Opens an existing PDF file.\& Returns a \fBfile\fR object or \fBnil, err\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&create(filename [, version])\fR
.RS 4
Creates a new PDF file.\& \fBversion\fR defaults to "1.\&7".\& Returns a \fBfile\fR
object or \fBnil, err\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&create_output(callback [, version])\fR
.RS 4
Creates a PDF file streamed through a Lua \fBcallback(data)\fR function,
called for each chunk of output.\& Useful for building a PDF entirely
in memory.\& Returns a \fBfile\fR object or \fBnil, err\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&create_temporary([version])\fR
.RS 4
Creates a PDF file backed by a unique temporary file.\& Returns a
\fBfile\fR object and the temporary filename, or \fBnil, err\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&array_create(pdf)\fR
.RS 4
Creates a new PDF array associated with the given \fBpdf\fR file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&create_icc_obj_from_file(pdf, filename, num_colors)\fR,
\fBpdfio.\&create_icc_obj_from_data(pdf, data, num_colors)\fR
.RS 4
Creates an ICC color profile object from a file or in\-memory data.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpdfio.\&create_color_from_icc_obj(pdf, icc_obj)\fR,
\fBpdfio.\&create_color_from_standard(pdf, num_colors, cs)\fR,
\fBpdfio.\&create_color_from_palette(pdf, num_colors, colors)\fR,
\fBpdfio.\&create_color_from_matrix(pdf, num_colors, gamma, matrix, white_point)\fR,
\fBpdfio.\&create_color_from_primaries(pdf, num_colors, gamma, wx, wy, rx, ry, gx, gy, bx, by)\fR
.RS 4
Create a PDF color space array: ICC\-based, standard (\fBcs\fR is one of
\fBpdfio.\&CS_ADOBE\fR, \fBpdfio.\&CS_P3_D65\fR, \fBpdfio.\&CS_SRGB\fR, or
\fBpdfio.\&CS_CGATS001\fR), indexed palette, calibrated matrix, or
primaries\-based, respectively.\& \fBmatrix\fR is a 3x3 table and
\fBwhite_point\fR a 3\-element table for the matrix variant.\&
.PP
.RE
All of the functions above are also available as \fBfile:\fR\fIname\fR(.\&.\&.\&)
methods (dropping the leading \fBpdf\fR argument), e.\&g.\&
\fBpdf:create_color_from_standard(3, pdfio.\&CS_SRGB)\fR.\&
.PP
.SH FILE METHODS
.PP
\fBfile:close()\fR
.RS 4
Closes the PDF file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_num_pages()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the number of pages in the PDF.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_page(n)\fR
.RS 4
Returns the \fBobj\fR for page \fBn\fR (0\-indexed).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_page([dict])\fR
.RS 4
Creates a new page and returns its \fBstream\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:find_obj(number)\fR
.RS 4
Looks up an existing indirect object by its object number.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:copy_obj(src_obj)\fR
.RS 4
Copies an object from another \fBfile\fR into this one, returning the
new object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:copy_page(src_page)\fR
.RS 4
Copies a page object from another \fBfile\fR into this one.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_permissions()\fR
.RS 4
Returns \fBpermissions, encryption\fR for an encrypted file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:set_permissions(permissions, encryption, owner_password, user_password)\fR
.RS 4
Enables encryption on a file being created, with the given
permission bits (\fBpdfio.\&PERMISSION_PRINT\fR, \fBpdfio.\&PERMISSION_COPY\fR,
etc.\&) and encryption mode (\fBpdfio.\&ENCRYPTION_AES_128\fR, etc.\&).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:dict_create()\fR
.RS 4
Creates a new PDF dictionary associated with this file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_array_obj(array)\fR, \fBfile:create_name_obj(name)\fR,
\fBfile:create_number_obj(num)\fR, \fBfile:create_string_obj(s)\fR,
\fBfile:create_obj(dict)\fR
.RS 4
Low\-level helpers to wrap a value as a standalone indirect object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_font_obj_from_base(name)\fR
.RS 4
Creates a font object from one of the 14 standard PDF base fonts
(e.\&g.\& "Helvetica", "Courier").\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_font_obj_from_data(data, unicode)\fR
.RS 4
Embeds a font from in\-memory TrueType/OpenType data, without
touching the filesystem.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_image_obj_from_file(filename, interpolate)\fR
.RS 4
Creates an image object from a JPEG or PNG file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:create_image_obj_from_data(data, width, height, num_colors,
color_data, alpha, interpolate)\fR
.RS 4
Embeds an image from an in\-memory raw pixel buffer, without
touching the filesystem.\& \fBdata\fR must be at least
\fBwidth\fR \fB \fRheight\fB \fR (\fBnum_colors\fR + (\fBalpha\fR and 1 or 0)) bytes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_author()\fR, \fBfile:get_title()\fR, \fBfile:get_version()\fR, etc.\&
.RS 4
Standard metadata getters.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:set_author(v)\fR, \fBfile:set_title(v)\fR, \fBfile:set_creator(v)\fR,
\fBfile:set_subject(v)\fR, \fBfile:set_keywords(v)\fR
.RS 4
Standard metadata setters.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_language()\fR, \fBfile:set_language(v)\fR
.RS 4
Get/set the document language (\fB/Lang\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:get_id()\fR, \fBfile:get_name()\fR
.RS 4
Return the trailer \fBID\fR array and the file'\&s name, respectively.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:set_creation_date(t)\fR, \fBfile:set_modification_date(t)\fR
.RS 4
Set timestamps (Unix time).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:add_output_intent(subtype, condition, cond_id, reg_name, info,
profile)\fR
.RS 4
Adds an OutputIntent dictionary to the file catalog.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBfile:string_create(s)\fR
.RS 4
Interns a string in the file'\&s string pool, returning it unchanged.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OBJECT METHODS
.PP
\fBobj:get_type()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the object type string (e.\&g.\&, "Page", "Catalog").\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_subtype()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the object'\&s sub\-type name (e.\&g.\&, "Image" for an image
XObject).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_dict()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the \fBdict\fR associated with the object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_rect(key)\fR
.RS 4
Returns a rectangle table (\fBx1, y1, x2, y2\fR) for a rectangle\-valued
dictionary key, such as "MediaBox".\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_number()\fR, \fBobj:get_generation()\fR
.RS 4
Return the object'\&s number and generation, as used by
\fBfile:find_obj()\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_length()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the length of the object'\&s data stream, if any.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_name()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the object'\&s name, for Name\-type objects.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:get_num_streams()\fR
.RS 4
Returns the number of content streams for a page object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:open_page_stream(n, decode)\fR
.RS 4
Opens a page'\&s \fBn\fRth content stream for reading.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:open_stream(decode)\fR
.RS 4
Opens a non\-page object'\&s data stream for reading.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:create_stream([filter])\fR
.RS 4
Creates a writable data stream for the object, optionally applying
a compression \fBfilter\fR (\fBpdfio.\&FILTER_FLATE\fR, etc.\&).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:image_get_width()\fR, \fBobj:image_get_height()\fR,
\fBobj:image_get_bytes_per_line()\fR
.RS 4
Return dimensions of an image object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:text_measure(s, size)\fR
.RS 4
Measures the width of string \fBs\fR at point \fBsize\fR when set in this
font object.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBobj:close()\fR
.RS 4
Closes the object (e.\&g.\& finishes writing its stream).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH DICTIONARY METHODS
.PP
\fBdict[key]\fR
.RS 4
Retrieves a value from the dictionary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdict:keys()\fR
.RS 4
Returns a table containing all keys in the dictionary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdict:iterate_keys(fn)\fR
.RS 4
Calls \fBfn(key)\fR for each key; stops early if \fBfn\fR returns \fBfalse\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdict:set_number(key, val)\fR, \fBdict:set_string(key, val)\fR, etc.\&
.RS 4
Sets values in the dictionary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdict:add_font(name, font_obj)\fR, \fBdict:add_image(name, image_obj)\fR,
\fBdict:add_color_space(name, array)\fR
.RS 4
Register a font, image, or color space object as a named page
resource.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdict:copy(pdf)\fR, \fBdict:clear(key)\fR
.RS 4
Copies the dictionary into another file, or removes a key.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ARRAY METHODS
.PP
\fBarray[n]\fR
.RS 4
Retrieves the \fBn\fRth element (1\-indexed).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB#array\fR
.RS 4
Returns the number of elements in the array.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarray:append_number(val)\fR, \fBarray:append_string(val)\fR,
\fBarray:append_boolean(val)\fR, \fBarray:append_date(val)\fR,
\fBarray:append_name(val)\fR, \fBarray:append_binary(val)\fR,
\fBarray:append_array(val)\fR, \fBarray:append_dict(val)\fR,
\fBarray:append_obj(val)\fR
.RS 4
Append a value of the corresponding type to the array.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarray:remove(n)\fR
.RS 4
Removes the \fBn\fRth element (1\-indexed).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarray:copy(pdf)\fR
.RS 4
Copies the array into another file, returning the new array.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH STREAM METHODS
.PP
\fBstream:read([amt])\fR
.RS 4
Reads data from the stream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:write(data)\fR
.RS 4
Writes data to the stream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:puts(s)\fR, \fBstream:putchar(ch)\fR
.RS 4
Write raw, unformatted data to the stream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:peek([amt])\fR, \fBstream:consume(bytes)\fR
.RS 4
Look ahead in the stream without advancing, or skip bytes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:get_token()\fR
.RS 4
Reads the next whitespace\-delimited PDF content token.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:close()\fR
.RS 4
Closes the stream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:draw_image(name, x, y, w, h)\fR
.RS 4
Draws a named image resource at the given position and size.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:text_begin()\fR, \fBstream:text_end()\fR, \fBstream:text_show(unicode, s)\fR
.RS 4
Text drawing functions.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:set_text_font(name, size)\fR, \fBstream:set_text_matrix(m)\fR,
\fBstream:set_text_word_spacing(spacing)\fR, \fBstream:set_text_character_spacing(spacing)\fR,
\fBstream:set_text_leading(leading)\fR, \fBstream:set_text_rendering_mode(mode)\fR,
\fBstream:set_text_rise(rise)\fR, \fBstream:set_text_x_scaling(percent)\fR
.RS 4
Text state setters.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:text_move_to(tx, ty)\fR, \fBstream:text_move_line(tx, ty)\fR,
\fBstream:text_new_line()\fR, \fBstream:text_next_line()\fR,
\fBstream:text_show_justified(unicode, fragments)\fR,
\fBstream:text_new_line_show(ws, cs, unicode, s)\fR
.RS 4
Additional text positioning and drawing functions.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBstream:path_rect(x, y, w, h)\fR, \fBstream:path_move_to(x, y)\fR,
\fBstream:path_line_to(x, y)\fR, \fBstream:path_curve(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3)\fR,
\fBstream:path_curve13(x1, y1, x3, y3)\fR, \fBstream:path_curve23(x2, y2, x3, y3)\fR,
\fBstream:path_close()\fR, \fBstream:path_end()\fR
.RS 4
Path construction functions.\& \fBpath_curve13\fR omits the second control
